From 668ad1d22b399d3597624412632c9853adf17135 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:01:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Finite strain behaviours: option to give the displacement
 gradient

FiniteStrainBehaviourOptions::gradient selects the gradient given to a
finite strain behaviour: the deformation gradient F (by default) or the
displacement gradient H = F - I. In single precision, F is only known
within about 6e-8, while H keeps the relative precision of small
strains.

With H:
- load checks that the behaviour accepts it (symbol
  <function>_AcceptsDisplacementGradient), offsets the stress measure
  by 10 and names the gradient DisplacementGradient;
- the initial states are zero instead of the identity;
- FiniteStrainSupport computes F = I + H;
- usesDisplacementGradient tells if a behaviour was loaded this way.

The test compares the integrations with F and with H for all the stress
measures and tangent operators, point by point and by batch, checks
the precision against analytical solutions (plane stress included) and
the initialize functions and post-processings. It is built when TFEL
supports the option.
