diff --git a/docs/web/bindings-cxx.md b/docs/web/bindings-cxx.md
index 793c9dd..45da285 100644
--- a/docs/web/bindings-cxx.md
+++ b/docs/web/bindings-cxx.md
@@ -166,6 +166,33 @@ o.tangent_operator = FiniteStrainBehaviourOptions::DPK1_DF;
 const auto b = load(o, 'src/libBehaviour.so', 'Norton', h);
 ~~~~
 
+The `gradient` option selects the gradient given to the behaviour:
+
+- `DEFORMATION_GRADIENT` (by default), the deformation gradient
+  $\boldsymbol{F}$;
+- `DISPLACEMENT_GRADIENT`, the displacement gradient
+  $\boldsymbol{H}=\boldsymbol{F}-\boldsymbol{I}$.
+
+The deformation gradient being close to the identity, its components
+are only known within about $6\,10^{-8}$ in single precision. The
+displacement gradient keeps the relative precision of small strains: the
+behaviours written in the Green-Lagrange or Hencky strain frameworks
+compute their strain from it without cancellation, and the behaviours
+written with the deformation gradient receive
+$\boldsymbol{F}=\boldsymbol{I}+\boldsymbol{H}$. The gradient of the loaded
+behaviour is then named `DisplacementGradient`, the states start from a
+zero displacement gradient, and the `usesDisplacementGradient` function
+returns `true`. This option requires a behaviour generated by a version
+of `MFront` which accepts it: `load` reports an error otherwise.
+
+~~~~{.cxx}
+o.gradient = FiniteStrainBehaviourOptions::DISPLACEMENT_GRADIENT;
+const auto b2 = load(o, "src/libBehaviour.so", "HenckyElasticity", h);
+~~~~
+
+Here, `HenckyElasticity` is a behaviour written in the Hencky strain
+framework, which benefits the most from this option.
+
 ## The `Behaviour` object
 
 The `Behaviour` object contains all the metadata required to interact
