+/*!
+ * \file   tests/DisplacementGradientTest.cxx
+ * \brief  Finite strain behaviours given the displacement gradient
+ * \f(H = F - I\f) instead of the deformation gradient \f(F\f) (option
+ * `gradient` of `FiniteStrainBehaviourOptions`):
+ *
+ * - description of the loaded behaviour and initial states;
+ * - integration point by point (`generic` interface) and by batch
+ *   (`generic-parallel` interface), for all the stress measures and tangent
+ *   operators, compared with the integration with the deformation gradient
+ *   (same results in double);
+ * - precision for small strains, compared with an analytical solution
+ *   computed in double: in single precision, the strain measures computed
+ *   from the displacement gradient keep the relative precision of the
+ *   strain, whereas the ones computed from the deformation gradient only
+ *   know it within about 6e-8 in absolute value;
+ * - conversions of `FiniteStrainSupport`;
+ * - plane stress, compared with an analytical solution;
+ * - initialize functions and post-processings, which shall receive the
+ *   options of the behaviour, point by point and by batch;
+ * - refusal of a small strain behaviour.
+ *
+ * The three behaviours are isotropic elastic behaviours: written with the
+ * deformation gradient (`SaintVenantKirchhoffElasticity`), and in the
+ * Green-Lagrange and Hencky strain frameworks (`GreenLagrangeElasticity`
+ * and `HenckyElasticity`, which also support plane stress and provide an
+ * initialize function and a post-processing).
